```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
    int n = sc.nextInt(); // number of pairs

    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      int a = sc.nextInt();
      int b = sc.nextInt();
      int sumSquared = (a + b) * (a + b);
      int squaredSum = a * a + b * b;

      if (sumSquared < squaredSum) {
        System.out.println("<");
      } else if (sumSquared > squaredSum) {
        System.out.println(">");
      } else {
        System.out.println("=");
      }
    }
    sc.close();
  }
}
```

we read the number of pairs, then loop through each pair. for each pair, we compute the sum of squares and the square of the sum. finally, we compare the two and print out '>', '<', or '=' based on the comparison result.

